WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.245 --> 00:00:14.080
[MUSIC]

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.800
Hello, my name is Nev Pierce. I'm Editor-At-Large for Empire

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:22.200
Magazine and I'm here to say as little as possible and

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:27.800
let this man do all the talking. Before you got into writing

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.100
professionally, there's this little period of time where

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.300
you worked on political campaigns, is that correct? How

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.400
did you get involved in that? It's not a clear trajectory.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.400
Like I did this, then I worked in politics, then I did this.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.700
So, in the midst around that time, I was writing that first

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.300
play my best friend a guy named Jay Carson, he's the

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.400
character Steve in Ides of March, and Farragut

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.400
North is based on him. He was having this meteoric rise

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.100
that already began in college and he said 'I'm working on

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.800
the Senate campaign. Why don't you come work on it?' And

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.800
I did, and I had a blast. It was an amazing experience.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.100
We were all over the state, you know, a couple twenty-year-

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.600
old guys feeling like, in our own infinite small way, we

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.500
were we were going to make a difference and make history,

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.800
and we won that race. And it was amazing. I mean, there's

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.400
very few things in life where, you know, on a particular

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.400
day at a particular time, whether you have succeeded or

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.100
failed and in an election is one of those things. And it's,

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.000
as I learned at that time, such a rush, such a high, when

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.700
you win. And as I learned later, so crushing when you lose.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:35.100
It's very black and white, but we won and I wanted more,

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:39.200
and that led to Hillary Clinton's Senate race in 2000, Bill

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.900
Bradley's presidential in 2000, and ultimately Howard Dean's

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.600
presidential in 2004, which is the last campaign I've ever

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.700
worked on, I guess over ten years ago now. And I drew from

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:55.300
all those experiences to write Farragut and  continue

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.100
to draw on them to write House of Cards, but politics was

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.800
never lik a 'thing' for me. I'm not a political junkie.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.400
I've written 12 plays and only one of them has to do

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.500
with politics. And, you know, the reason you guys probably

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.600
showed up is because of House of Cards and so, the two

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.500
things that I'm most known for, Farragut North and Ides

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.900
of March on the one hand and House of Cards in the other

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.000
both are in the world of politics, but that's

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:27.700
not a subject that interests me. Power. No, I'm

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.910
not trying to be cavalier here. Power really interests me.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:36.200
Politics is a subset of power and politics in Washington

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:40.500
at this level, you're seeing power explored in the most

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.800
sophisticated way with the highest stakes,

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:48.800
but I'm just as interested in fascinated by the power relationship,

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.900
within the marriage between Frank and Claire Underwood,

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.200
which is the real subject of the show, not politics, if

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.200
that makes sense. So, can we talk a little bit about how

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.500
how closely Farragut was to your own experience or your

